node_modules/
.next/
.env*
!.env.example
# Build configuration, not credentials: it holds one flag that puts the
# deployed frontend into mock mode, because a static deployment has no
# backend behind it. It has to be committed or the hosted build has no way
# to know that. A platform env var still overrides it — Vite applies
# process.env over .env files — so pointing a deployment at a real API
# later needs no code change.
!frontend/.env.production
